  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 217 AM MDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nWill have warm and dry weather today with continued warming on\nsoutherly flow aloft. Will see upper 70s to lower 80s in the \nvalleys and 60s and 70s in higher elevations. A cold front will\napproach FRiday with windy conditions in the central mountains\nwith 25 to 35 mph wind gusts expected. Won't be quite as windy\nin the Snake Plain and southern mountains but still expecting 20\nto 30 mph wind gusts down there as well. Will remain very\nwarm with highs again in the upper 70s to lower 80s valleys.\nWill see significant cooling Saturday with highs near normal in\nthe 60s mountains and upper 60s to near 70 in valleys. An upper\nlevel trof will move through Sunday and will have a slight\nchance of showers and thunderstorms mainly in the mountains\nSunday into Monday. After warming up again through Sunday will\nsee some slight cooling again Monday into next week with below\nnormal highs Monday through Wednesday. Expecting dry conditions\nTuesday through Thursday.",
